    {
      "id": "60dij-S8tGWpzA1qEKIBq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1878.5171994599016,
      "y": 2568.4156170118345,
      "width": 706.8472900390625,
      "height": 480,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 555105043,
      "version": 1185,
      "versionNonce": 475275507,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789812320907,
      "created": 1789750845170,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements\n\n- multiple jobs can be run at same time by different customers\n- customers can only see their scheduled jobs (quota limits apply)\n- Customers can schedule jobs from minutes into the future up to 1 year ahead.\n- Customers can configure maximum retries and a backoff policy.\n- The customer must explicitly choose a concurrency policy:\nALLOW_CONCURRENT\nSKIP_IF_RUNNING\nQUEUE\n- Customers can pause/resume or permanently disable a schedule.\nA currently running execution is not automatically terminated when the schedule is paused.\n- How changes in a job schedule affects an active job?\n\nSystem Behaviour\n- Report success or failure after completion\n- Can retry jobs. \nRetries are executions of the same logical job.\nThey must respect the job's concurrency policy.\n- How is the scheduler executing the job: api, via specifying endpoint, method,payload\n- Multiple jobs scheduled at same time, need to run all at same time\n- can a delay accetable (+-10 seconds) while starting the job, can expect more in load but\nno skipping, delivery at least one execution\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements\n\n- multiple jobs can be run at same time by different customers\n- customers can only see their scheduled jobs (quota limits apply)\n- Customers can schedule jobs from minutes into the future up to 1 year ahead.\n- Customers can configure maximum retries and a backoff policy.\n- The customer must explicitly choose a concurrency policy:\nALLOW_CONCURRENT\nSKIP_IF_RUNNING\nQUEUE\n- Customers can pause/resume or permanently disable a schedule.\nA currently running execution is not automatically terminated when the schedule is paused.\n- How changes in a job schedule affects an active job?\n\nSystem Behaviour\n- Report success or failure after completion\n- Can retry jobs. \nRetries are executions of the same logical job.\nThey must respect the job's concurrency policy.\n- How is the scheduler executing the job: api, via specifying endpoint, method,payload\n- Multiple jobs scheduled at same time, need to run all at same time\n- can a delay accetable (+-10 seconds) while starting the job, can expect more in load but\nno skipping, delivery at least one execution\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_K1iLxjEsdWeG7dLw0MZW",
